---
import Lockup from './Lockup.astro';

const year = new Date().getUTCFullYear();

const groups = [
  {
    heading: 'Product',
    links: [
      { href: '/product', label: 'Signal Protocol SDK' },
      /* "Demo in your browser" pointed at /demo and is gone with the route.
         The scenarios are a homepage section now, and a footer link to a
         fragment of the page the logo above already links to is the kind of
         entry a footer accumulates rather than earns. */
      /* One entry, not two. This sat above a "Security review pack" link to
         /evaluate until that page folded into this one, and a footer column
         listing the same destination twice under two names is worse than the
         split it replaced. */
      { href: '/security', label: 'Security model and review pack' },
      { href: '/pricing', label: 'Pricing' },
      { href: '/licensing', label: 'Licensing' },
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Build',
    links: [
      { href: 'https://docs.open-e2ee.dev/start/quickstart', label: 'Ten-minute quickstart' },
      { href: 'https://docs.open-e2ee.dev', label: 'Documentation' },
      { href: 'https://github.com/open-e2ee/signal-protocol-js', label: 'SDK on GitHub' },
      { href: 'https://github.com/open-e2ee/signal-protocol-js/blob/main/docs/SECURITY.md', label: 'Threat model' },
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Learn',
    links: [
      { href: '/learn', label: 'How E2EE changes your architecture' },
      { href: '/blog', label: 'Blog' },
      { href: 'https://console.open-e2ee.dev', label: 'Console' },
      { href: 'mailto:licensing@open-e2ee.dev', label: 'Contact' },
    ],
  },
];
---

<footer class="site-footer">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="footer-grid">
      <div class="footer-brand">
        <a class="brand-link" href="/"><Lockup /></a>
        {/*
          The footer carried "Opaque to the relay. Open to inspection." and,
          under it, "Brand language is provisional — taglines are proposed,
          pending sign-off." Both are gone, by founder decision on 2026-08-04,
          and the tagline itself is still undecided: `docs/decisions.md` §1
          stays open. Dropping the line is not approving or rejecting it.

          Two reasons, and the second is the one that matters. The note was
          internal process copy — our own review state, shipped to every
          visitor on every page of the site, answering a question no customer
          asked. And "Opaque" is an absolute the rest of this site spends its
          effort not making: the carrier panel on the landing page prints
          `senderUserId alice` in the clear, and the fixed relay formula is
          deliberately narrower — the relay never needs message plaintext or
          device private keys. A brand line that overstates against our own
          published evidence is the one kind of copy this project cannot
          afford, whoever signs it off.

          The design contract requires an annotation only from a surface that
          *uses* a tagline, so a footer without one owes nothing. `/product`
          still does — its h1 is the proposed Product hero string — and that
          page now carries the annotation itself, scoped to the one page that
          needs it. See `src/pages/product.astro`.
        */}
        <p>
          Open-source, protocol-level end-to-end encryption SDKs for TypeScript developers. AGPL-3.0
          for open source; commercial licenses for proprietary products.
        </p>
      </div>
      {groups.map((group) => (
        <div>
          <h2>{group.heading}</h2>
          <nav aria-label={group.heading}>
            {group.links.map((link) => <a href={link.href}>{link.label}</a>)}
          </nav>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="footer-legal">
      <nav aria-label="Legal">
        <a href="/legal">Legal</a>
        <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy</a>
        <a href="/legal/terms">Terms</a>
      </nav>
      <p>© {year} OpenE2EE LLC and OpenE2EE contributors.</p>
      <p>
        An independent implementation of the published Signal Protocol specifications. Not
        affiliated with, endorsed by, or wire-compatible with Signal Messenger LLC or Signal
        Technology Foundation.
      </p>
      {/*
        Required, and quoted rather than paraphrased. OSI's guidelines give the
        sentence verbatim — "include the statement 'The OSI logo trademark is
        the trademark of Open Source Initiative.'" — and a trademark notice is
        the one kind of copy on this site with a correct wording that is not
        ours to improve. It also carries the ® acknowledgement for a mark shown
        without the logotype the ® is attached to.

        It sits in the footer on every page while the mark itself is on one,
        which is the same shape as the Signal note above it and the reason
        that note is above it: a reader looking for who owns what finds both in
        the same place. `tests/site-content.test.mjs` ties the two together from
        the other end — the landing page may not carry the keyhole without this
        line and the AGPL-3.0 statement being on the site.
      */}
      <p>The OSI logo trademark is the trademark of Open Source Initiative.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>
